 "notes": "Lane directions/speeds were identified per lane from the trained policy's hit rates and confirmed by the critic TD residual (0.113 best vs 0.136-0.27 for alternatives). Critic V(s0)=7.2 vs empirical discounted return 10.1: expected, the critic cannot see the step counter and PPO treated the 200-step cap as termination, so its value averages over the remaining horizon (~6.9 predicted for 0.12 reward/step); with prev0=zeros V(s0) drops to 1.6, which is why the start prev frame is taken to be a copy of the first frame. Weakly constrained details: the clock offset (t=0 vs a random offset gives the same stats; TD 0.113 vs 0.117), the swap-collision rule and reset-to-start vs reset-row-only (the trained policy almost never collides; only the random-policy return 0.010 vs ref 0.011 favours swap collisions, without them 0.017-0.025; push-back-one-row gives 0.03-0.055 and is rejected), and the start column (4 fits far better than 3, 5 or random). Collision penalty: none (ref random return is positive; -1 penalty would make it negative)."
